id: pm-yds9dt
title: Expose agent probe controls and versioned legacy-author vocabulary through pm config and SDK mutation APIs
description: "The new agent_identity.probes_enabled and identity_vocabulary settings are validated and consumed, but pm config cannot yet read or mutate them. Add typed project config keys and SDK mutation helpers for probe enablement, vocabulary version bumps, exact alias add/remove, clear, dry-run, and residual coverage preview without direct settings-file edits."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:config",cli,context-management,identity,provenance,sdk
created_at: "2026-08-02T23:03:26.452Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T11:33:11.828Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T11:33:11.222Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T11:33:11.222Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "pm config project get/list/export exposes probe policy and vocabulary revision/count without dumping unnecessary aliases; Typed CLI and SDK mutations add/remove exact aliases and monotonically update the vocabulary version through audited settings history; CLI, SDK, MCP, contracts, completions, docs, sparse settings compatibility, and temporary consumer tests remain in parity"
parent: pm-8jdc
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Shipped typed probe policy and versioned legacy-author vocabulary mutations across SDK, CLI, and MCP, including prototype-setter rejection and complete alias-test linkage."
expected_result: "Operators and integrations can get, preview, add, remove, and clear agent identity vocabulary without direct settings edits, alias disclosure, or false prototype-key mutations."
actual_result: "Sparse settings, monotonic revisioning, prototype-key rejection, residual counts, CLI, SDK, MCP parity, complete linked evidence, and exact 100 percent coverage verification pass."
