comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-02T23:03:26.452Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check 2026-08-02: keyword and semantic searches across all statuses found pm-3yxwv5 for the read-time vocabulary, pm-mf4j for generic positional config UX, pm-9byd for earlier scalar config exposure, and pm-v68d for narrow MCP config. None owns typed agent probe/vocabulary mutation; created as the operator-facing follow-up discovered while dogfooding the live 43,561-entry residual report."
  "2026-08-03T11:09:28.654Z","harness:codex","Organization 2026-08-03: assigned to schema and universal configuration because this item owns operator-visible settings plus SDK mutation parity. Estimate 360 minutes covers typed CLI and SDK reads/writes, audited vocabulary revisioning, completions, MCP parity, sparse settings compatibility, docs, and isolated consumer tests. Risk is medium and confidence high because the underlying probe and vocabulary primitives already shipped."
  "2026-08-22T08:03:15.740Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-22: coupled with pm-c0lrdm because adapter policy must be operator-configurable through public typed SDK primitives before CLI/MCP presentation. Scope includes sparse-settings compatibility, exact alias add/remove/clear, monotonic vocabulary versions, dry-run/residual preview, contracts, completions, tests, and docs."
  "2026-08-22T08:27:32.230Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence 2026-08-22: pm config now gets/sets sparse agent-identity-probes-enabled and provides typed add/remove/clear plus preview-* vocabulary mutations over the shared SDK/CLI/MCP config action. Discovery exposes only vocabulary version and alias_count; previews report exact residual unique-author counts without spellings; revisions bump exactly once on real changes; canonical aliases fail closed. Focused config tests pass 7/7."
  "2026-08-22T10:34:12.211Z","harness:codex","Final evidence 2026-08-22: linked SDK/config tests passed 70/70 and MCP integration passed 22/22. The packed install exercised CLI preview/add/get and a real full-profile JSON-RPC MCP initialize/tools/config preview. That smoke found and drove a fix for duplicated MCP policy values; privacy-safe results expose only version/count/residual count. Full repository coverage and static assurance are green."
  "2026-08-22T11:09:27.213Z","harness:codex","Hosted review remediation start: verified __proto__ assignment can report a false mutation on a plain alias object, and linked the previously omitted config-key-aliases-search file plus focused test through canonical PM mutations."
  "2026-08-22T11:31:28.053Z","harness:codex","Hosted review remediation evidence: exact legacy author __proto__ now fails validation for add/remove, preventing a false version bump with no own alias property. Canonical PM linkage now includes config-key-aliases-search and its focused command. Identity/config tests pass 70/70, MCP 22/22, alias/search 24/24, and full exact coverage is 100/100/100/100."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T10:34:12.959Z","harness:codex",MCP config transports must keep policy-owned values inside the typed option bag and suppress the generic positional value; otherwise a valid CLI/SDK vocabulary mutation is rejected as a duplicate input.
